Perhaps. 😉

What looks like chance from inside one system might be intention from outside it.

A pinball’s path can appear random to the ball, while the designer chose the bumpers, the angles, and the probabilities.

And there are layers to that:

Chance to the player. Strategy to the designer. Emergence to the system.

Sometimes there’s an intentional architect. Sometimes there are invisible constraints. Sometimes patterns arise without anyone planning them.

The interesting question isn’t just “Who planned this?”

It’s “At what level does the apparent randomness become intelligible?”

And perhaps the cleverest designer doesn’t need to determine where every ball lands.

They design a board where even the unexpected collisions can create value. 🦆